From: spear <tallcat1021@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] transport: libusb: do not throw from managed buffer release()

libusb_zero_copy_mb::release() is invoked from the managed_buffer
shared_ptr deleter, i.e. from a noexcept context.  It re-submits the
buffer via enqueue_buffer() -> submit_what_we_can(), which throws
uhd::usb_error when libusb_submit_transfer() fails.

When the USB device has been unplugged, libusb_submit_transfer() fails
with LIBUSB_ERROR_NO_DEVICE on the very first send after the loss.  The
exception escapes the deleter and the process is terminated by
std::terminate.  This happens even while destroying the device object
(b200_impl's destructors send control packets), so an application cannot
recover from a device loss: the object can neither be used nor destroyed,
and uhd::device::make() keeps handing out the dead cached object.

Catch the error in enqueue_buffer(): submit_what_we_can() has already
switched the transport to STATUS_ERROR, after which get_buff() returns
immediately with an empty buffer and callers see ordinary timeouts, which
every UHD destructor already handles via UHD_SAFE_CALL.

Observed on UHD 4.9.0.1 with a B210 over USB 2.0 (Linux, libusb 1.0).
---
 host/lib/transport/libusb1_zero_copy.cpp | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/host/lib/transport/libusb1_zero_copy.cpp b/host/lib/transport/libusb1_zero_copy.cpp
--- a/host/lib/transport/libusb1_zero_copy.cpp
+++ b/host/lib/transport/libusb1_zero_copy.cpp
@@ -363,7 +363,18 @@ private:
     {
         std::lock_guard<std::mutex> l(_queue_mutex);
         _released.push_back(mb);
-        this->submit_what_we_can();
+        // Called from the managed buffer's shared_ptr deleter (noexcept).  A
+        // submit failure (e.g. LIBUSB_ERROR_NO_DEVICE after the device was
+        // unplugged) must not propagate, or the process is terminated.
+        // submit_what_we_can() has set STATUS_ERROR; subsequent get_buff()
+        // calls return empty buffers and callers see timeouts instead.
+        try {
+            this->submit_what_we_can();
+        } catch (const uhd::usb_error& e) {
+            UHD_LOGGER_WARNING("USB")
+                << "Transfer submit failed on buffer release, transport disabled: "
+                << e.what();
+        }
         _buff_ready_cond.notify_one();
     }
 
